Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: stage MT798x zero-wait DFS CAC

Stage an 80 MHz AP on the lower non-DFS block, start background CAC
on the adjacent upper block, then use CSA to reach the configured
80 or 160 MHz channel when it is available. Preserve ETSI CAC and
radar safeguards, including NOP checks before 160 MHz expansion.

This path is enabled only by enable_staged_zwdfs. "Staged" describes
the hostapd channel sequence: MT7986 uses adjacent TX80/RX160 while
MT7981 uses a dedicated RX path. RF behavior needs hardware validation
on both devices.
---
